<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Pay classification' }) %>
<div class="page-head"><div>
  <p class="crumb"><a href="/pc#talent">← People &amp; Culture</a></p>
  <h1>Pay classification</h1>
  <p class="sub">A person's role is their pay classification, not their job title. This is every scale payroll carries and the category it maps to.</p>
</div></div>

<% const t = scales.totals; %>
<div class="grid kpis">
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= t.scales %></div><div class="l">Pay scales in payroll</div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= t.people %></div><div class="l">People on them<span class="cap"><%= t.permanent %> permanent · <%= t.casual %> casual</span></div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n <%= t.unmapped_scales ? 'bad-text' : '' %>"><%= t.unmapped_scales %></div><div class="l">Scales no rule maps<span class="cap"><%= t.unmapped_people %> <%= t.unmapped_people === 1 ? 'person' : 'people' %>, counted as Unclassified</span></div></div>
  <div class="card stat"><div class="n"><%= t.no_scale_people %></div><div class="l">No classification recorded<span class="cap">counted as Unclassified; no rule is missing</span></div></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Every scale, and where it lands</h2>
  <% if (!scales.rows.length) { %>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:0;">No pay classifications have been read from payroll yet. They arrive with the nightly talent sync, or on demand with <code>npm run talent-snapshot</code>.</p>
  <% } else { %>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;"><table>
    <thead><tr>
      <th>Pay classification (payRateTemplate)</th>
      <th class="num">People</th>
      <th class="num">Permanent</th>
      <th class="num">Casual</th>
      <th>Category</th>
      <th>Matched on</th>
    </tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% scales.rows.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <tr>
        <td<%= r.recorded ? '' : ' class="muted"' %>><%= r.label %></td>
        <td class="num" style="font-weight:700;"><%= r.people %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= r.permanent %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= r.casual %></td>
        <td><strong><%= r.category_label %></strong><% if (!r.matched) { %> <span class="tag-fut" title="No rule in services/classification.js matches this scale">unmapped</span><% } %></td>
        <td class="small muted"><%= r.why %><% if (r.stale) { %> · <span class="tag-fut" title="The rule has changed since the last payroll sync; this page shows the current rule">rule changed since the last sync</span><% } %></td>
      </tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="footnote">
    Counts are the people employed as at the last payroll sync<% if (locals.talentSync && talentSync.last_attempt) { %> (<%= talentSync.last_attempt %>)<% } %>; the category beside each scale is the rule as it stands right now.
    Permanent and casual come from payroll's employment type, not from the word in the scale's name.
    <% if (t.no_scale_people) { %>The people payroll records no classification for are the unnamed row above, and are not counted as a scale.<% } %>
  </p>
  <% } %>
</div>

<% if (scales.rows.length) { %>
<details class="card working">
  <summary><strong>The categories</strong> — what each one adds up to</summary>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-top:10px;"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th class="num">People</th><th class="num">Scales</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% scales.byCategory.forEach(function(c){ %>
      <tr><td><%= c.label %></td><td class="num"><%= c.people %></td><td class="num"><%= c.scales %></td></tr>
      <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="footnote" style="margin-top:12px;">
    The rule reads the scale's <em>family</em> and its <em>level</em> separately, so a Casual CSE Level 5 lands where a Permanent CSE Level 5 does, and a suffix such as “17 yrs” does not break the match — while “Teachers … Level 3” and “CSE Level 3” stay the different scales they are. Teachers scales are ECT; CSE 1–2 Trainee, 3–4 Cert 3, 5–6 Dip, 7–8 Management; Support Worker scales are Support (their L1.1 is a support-worker step, never a CSE level); anything else is Unclassified.
  </p>
</details>
<% } %>

<p class="footnote">
  Read-only. The mapping lives in <code>services/classification.js</code>; changing it is a code change, then a talent sync. This page exists so a scale that is unmapped or in the wrong category can be seen rather than inferred from a number that looks wrong.
</p>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
